<section class="page-section section-rule soft-section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-heading compact-heading"><p class="kicker">Ways to contribute</p><h2>Begin where you are.</h2></div>
    <div class="contribute-grid">
      <article><span>Economists</span><h3>Propose and clarify theory</h3><p>Bring research questions and models, identify assumptions worth comparing, and connect formal statements to the economic literature.</p></article>
      <article><span>Lean users</span><h3>Formalize and review</h3><p>Develop reusable definitions and proofs, improve APIs, test examples, and review code. Read the <a href="{{ site.repository }}/blob/{{ site.sourceBranch }}/CONTRIBUTING.md">contribution guide</a> for build requirements, API changes, and review.</p></article>
      <article><span>New contributors</span><h3>Read, ask, and document</h3><p>Work through the <a href="{{ site.repository }}/blob/{{ site.sourceBranch }}/docs/BeginnersManual.md">beginner’s manual</a>, report unclear points, improve explanations, or discuss a small task in <a href="{{ site.issues }}">GitHub Issues</a>. Small, well-scoped additions to <code>ForMathlib/</code> can also be suitable first contributions.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="contact-strip">
      <div><h2>Start a conversation</h2><p>For questions about the mathematics, Lean code, documentation, or project direction, write to contact@mathecon.dev. Use GitHub Issues for bugs and scoped work.</p></div>
      <a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:contact@mathecon.dev">Email MathEconLib <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
