<section class="page-section section-rule" id="research-projects">
  <div class="shell editorial-grid">
    <div class="sticky-label">Research projects</div>
    <div class="prose-large">
      <h2>Propose a focused project.</h2>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:contact@mathecon.dev">contact@mathecon.dev</a> or open a <a href="{{ site.issues }}">design issue</a>. Describe the economic question and relevant literature, the intended definitions and assumptions, the main statement or example to formalize, and the existing library components you expect to reuse.</p>
      <p>Changes to foundational layers, or a new foundational layer, start with a design issue and agreement on the definitions and main statements before writing proofs. Follow the <a href="{{ site.repository }}/blob/{{ site.sourceBranch }}/DESIGN.md">design principles</a>; PRs touching core layers require a maintainer review before merge.</p>
      <p>New theorems in existing chapters, documentation, and applications built on existing layers can go straight to a focused pull request under the <a href="{{ site.repository }}/blob/{{ site.sourceBranch }}/CONTRIBUTING.md">contribution guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
